      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "IDEAL TIMING (1) failed to fire last start when having drawn out wide was restrained to race well back in the running and only battled in the run home to finish seventh at Bathurst over 1730m. He has won two of his last four starts and from the inside draw today should be returning to top-three form. ALERT BAY (4) after having placed in all of his five previous runs scored a well deserved win by a neck as the favourite over 1609m last start after having raced outside the leader and then taking over the front with 400m to run. Racing well and looks well placed to go back-to-back. MICK DANGER (7) did well to place third here last start over 2300m when after racing four-back on the fence came home after he was held-up into the turn. Each-way claims. GRAYSON RED (5) is the best of the rest after finishing third at long odds over 1730m at Bathurst last time out after he raced three-back on the fence for most of the trip.",
